    <string name="monet_impression_title">Impression, Sunrise</string>
    <string name="monet_impression_note">The port of Le Havre at dawn. A critic mocked the title, and the word “Impressionism” was born.</string>
    <string name="monet_nympheas_title">Water Lilies</string>
    <string name="monet_nympheas_note">Monet painted the water lilies of his Giverny pond more than 250 times, at every hour of the day.</string>
    <string name="monet_prairie_title">Meadow at Giverny</string>
    <string name="monet_prairie_note">Settled in Giverny, Monet painted the countryside around his house in every light, before creating his famous water garden.</string>
    <string name="panier_pommes_title">The Basket of Apples</string>
    <string name="panier_pommes_year">c. 1893</string>
    <string name="panier_pommes_note">The table tilts, and so does the bottle: Cézanne shows each object from its best angle, even if perspective bends.</string>
    <string name="voyageur_brume_title">Wanderer above the Sea of Fog</string>
    <string name="voyageur_brume_year">c. 1818</string>
    <string name="voyageur_brume_note">The icon of German Romanticism. We never see the wanderer\'s face: we look out over the fog with him.</string>
    <string name="pont_neuf_title">The Pont Neuf</string>
    <string name="pont_neuf_note">Renoir painted the crowd from the upper floor of a café; his brother stopped passers-by to make them pause for a moment.</string>
    <string name="grande_jatte_title">A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte</string>
    <string name="grande_jatte_note">Two years of work, dot by dot: Seurat sets touches of pure colour side by side for the eye to blend from afar.</string>
    <string name="noce_juive_title">Jewish Wedding in Morocco</string>
    <string name="noce_juive_year">c. 1839</string>
    <string name="noce_juive_note">Delacroix attended this celebration in Tangier in 1832 and painted it from memory, helped by his sketchbooks.</string>
    <string name="vermeer_laitiere_title">The Milkmaid</string>
    <string name="vermeer_laitiere_year">c. 1658</string>
    <string name="vermeer_laitiere_note">A trickle of milk, a ray of light: Vermeer turns a kitchen gesture into a moment held still.</string>
    <string name="american_gothic_title">American Gothic</string>
    <string name="american_gothic_note">Wood posed his sister and his dentist in front of an Iowa house. People take them for husband and wife; he meant father and daughter.</string>
    <string name="liberte_peuple_title">Liberty Leading the People</string>
    <string name="liberte_peuple_note">Painted to honour the July Revolution of 1830. Restored in 2024, it has regained its bright colours.</string>
    <string name="naissance_venus_title">The Birth of Venus</string>
    <string name="naissance_venus_year">c. 1485</string>
    <string name="naissance_venus_note">Zephyr blows the goddess towards the shore, where one of the Horae waits with a flowered cloak.</string>
    <string name="joconde_title">Mona Lisa</string>
    <string name="joconde_artist">Leonardo da Vinci</string>
    <string name="joconde_nickname">Leonardo</string>
    <string name="joconde_note">Leonardo kept it all his life and kept retouching it. Her smile owes everything to sfumato, outlines melting into shadow.</string>
